# Cache headers for Workers Static Assets (2026-10-13, the owner's
# "always live" rule made explicit):
#
#  - /assets/* are content-hashed by the build — a new deploy changes every
#    hash, so a year-long immutable cache is ALWAYS correct while removing a
#    revalidation round trip per asset. The HTML is the source of truth and
#    it always revalidates, so a cached asset can only ever be one the live
#    HTML itself references.
#  - The document (index.html + the single-page-application fallback paths)
#    and the service worker revalidate on every request — visitors always
#    get the deployed version, and sw.js updates land on the next
#    navigation. (Workers Assets already send `max-age=0, must-revalidate`
#    for HTML by default; restated so the intent survives config drift.)
#  - /api, /internal and /admin are Worker-first paths and set their own
#    headers — untouched here.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
